    "title": {
      "source": "收获",
      "en": "Harvest"
    },
    "caption": {
      "source": "作品内容：\n1*马首（我在天空中奔跑，一片片云浪遮盖住我的身体，此时它们和我是一体的。我望向远处，正午的阳光的确很耀眼，鹰追逐着光往高处越飞越远…）\n2*鹰盾（我把羽毛做成项链戴在脖颈上，今天我将作为信使，带着收获的麦穗去传达福音，传达爱）\n3*平打手镯（一对恪守初心的羽翼，守护着沙漏，守护着最初的梦。时间验证了一切，鹰幻做使者传达福音，送来了收获的麦穗。#镯体≈14.5，开口≈3cm）\n4*缰绳戒指（金与银，十字浮出与镂空，神圣的样子。#港码≈17码）\n5*S十字（秋日的麦穗在十字的画框里起舞，收获的喜悦洋溢在它的脸上）",
      "en": "The pieces:\n1* Horse head (I run through the sky. Waves of cloud cover my body; now they and I are one. I look into the distance: the midday sunlight is indeed dazzling, and an eagle follows the light, flying ever higher and farther...)\n2* Eagle shield (I made feathers into a necklace and put it around my neck. Today I will be a messenger, carrying harvested ears of wheat to bring the good news, to bring love)\n3* Flat-forged cuff (a pair of Wings stays true to its first intention, guarding the hourglass, guarding the earliest dream. Time has proven it all; the eagle becomes a messenger to bring the good news, delivering harvested ears of wheat. #Body approx. 14.5, opening approx. 3cm)\n4 * Rein ring (gold and silver, raised and openwork crosses, a sacred form; Hong Kong size approx. 17)\n5* S Cross (autumn ears of wheat dance within the cross-shaped frame, the joy of harvest all over its face)"
    },
