  "legacy:2023-067-d03b3f8e07": {
    "title": {
      "source": "Merry Christma！",
      "en": "Merry Christma！"
    },
    "caption": {
      "source": "Through hill and valley every breezeHad sunk to rest with folded wings:Keen was the air, but could not freeze,Nor check, the music of the strings;So stout and hardy were the bandThat scraped the chords with strenuous hand.\nAnd who but listened?…\n\"Merry Christmas\" wished to all.\n穿过山谷的每一阵微风下沉收起翅膀：风是那么锋利，但永不冷漠，也不核对，弦音声声；一层层又如此的强烈刚强，用热烈的手摩擦着弦柱。这一刻是谁在倾听？\n祝福大家：❄️圣诞快乐呀❄️\n——William Wordsworth 《The Minstrels》",
      "en": "Through hill and valley every breezeHad sunk to rest with folded wings:Keen was the air, but could not freeze,Nor check, the music of the strings;So stout and hardy were the bandThat scraped the chords with strenuous hand.\nAnd who but listened?…\n\"Merry Christmas\" wished to all.\nEvery breeze passing through the valley sinks down and folds its wings: the wind is so sharp, yet never indifferent, nor does it cross-check; the strings sound on and on. Layer upon layer, so strong and unyielding, rubbing the tuning pegs with fervent hands. Who is listening at this moment?\nWishing everyone: ❄️Merry Christmas❄️\n——William Wordsworth 《The Minstrels》"
    },
    "heading": {
      "source": "Merry Christma！",
      "en": "Merry Christma！"
    },
    "lead": {
      "source": "",
      "en": ""
    }
  },
